cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this teaching package, please cite it as below."

title: "Beyond the Optimum: Chemical Engineering Decisions with Multiple Objectives and Uncertainty"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Zondervan"
    given-names: "Edwin"

affiliation: "University of Twente"

date-released: "2026-09-01"

abstract: >
  A MATLAB teaching example for superstructure-based process design,
  multi-objective optimization, Pareto analysis, epsilon-constraint
  optimization, decision-making under uncertainty, and minimax-regret
  analysis using a simplified low-carbon methanol process example.

keywords:
  - process systems engineering
  - superstructure optimization
  - mathematical programming
  - multi-objective optimization
  - Pareto optimization
  - epsilon-constraint method
  - uncertainty
  - minimax regret
  - methanol
  - MATLAB

license: MIT

repository-code: "https://github.com/zondervanedwin-collab/beyond-the-optimum"
url: "https://github.com/zondervanedwin-collab/beyond-the-optimum"
